<title>JAPAN: Japan October vehicle exports up 17.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan October vehicle exports up 17.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle exports rose 17.3 percent in October from a year earlier to 321,302 units, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the fifth successive month exports had gained on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>				  OCT	  YR/YR CHANGE</p>
<p> Cars			248,754	    +20.9</p>
<p> Trucks		     69,200	     +6.9</p>
<p> Buses			 3,348	     -5.5</p>
<p> Total		     321,302	    +17.3</p>
<p>Exports by destination:</p>
<p> Asia			 49,244	     -0.6</p>
<p> Mideast		    28,704	    +54.7</p>
<p> Europe		     73,489	     -2.1</p>
<p> - EU			 59,323	     -8.2</p>
<p> North America	   110,178	    +38.6</p>
<p> - U.S.		    103,098	    +35.9</p>
<p> Latin America	    26,678	    +21.8</p>
<p> Africa			9,587	    +15.3</p>
<p> Oceania		    22,727	    +11.4</p>
<p> Other			   695	     -3.7</p>
<p>Exports by major manufacturers:</p>
<p> Toyota	 124,145	    +27.2</p>
<p> Nissan	  48,839	     +3.2</p>
<p> Mazda	   36,541	    +40.3</p>
<p> Honda	   34,115	    +27.7</p>
<p> Mitsubishi    34,012	     +5.8</p>
